 ### Dev tools: which lock file for which OS
 `requirements-dev.txt` is the authority: Linux x86_64, Python 3.12 (CI and containers). `requirements-dev-win.txt` is the Windows lock (Python 3.13, made with `uv pip compile requirements-dev.in --generate-hashes --python-version 3.13 --python-platform windows --no-strip-extras`); it has the same pins plus `colorama`. Install with `pip install --require-hashes -r <that file>`. Both files are regenerated together when `requirements-dev.in` changes. The browser tests have their own optional lock files, `requirements-browser.txt` and `requirements-browser-win.txt` (made from `requirements-browser.in`, see `versions.md`), installed after the development lock. Quality commands (all must pass): `ruff check .`, `ruff format --check .`, `mypy --platform linux`, `mypy --platform win32`, `bandit -ll -r src tools scripts -c pyproject.toml`, `python scripts/check_schema.py`.
